Z||000000||JayUSA77||07-28-2001||08:02 PM||||hey guys i have a black tinted window and it looks horible because of scratch marks all up and down the tint job. I took off my door panels and i know what it was, its the rubber weatherstrip which i have, and this other little part i need that i dont know the name of it.  Its at the very top of the door and its used for adjusting the windows back and forth. it has a little pad at the end that is supposed to be soft, but from many years of the window going up and down it seems to of gotten worn down to metal.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> There is 2 of them per window and i cant find them on the fierostore at all. what the hell are these called and where can i get them. thanks<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||mbramble||07-28-2001||09:43 PM||||They are called the front and rear stabilizer-to-inner door.  Check the local junkyards.  These <I>normally</I> don't get too worn because they are inside the window glass and out of most of the weather.||||reg||1
